{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to the glom library, focusing on new specification types for data transformation and improved CLI capabilities. It also refines internal representations and public API consistency across various spec classes.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The `glom_cli` command-line interface must accept Python-full specifications rather than being limited to AST literals, allowing for more complex logic in specs. The `mw_get_target` and `mw_handle_target` functions must correctly process targets that are AST literals or full Python expressions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "text": "The `Auto`, `Fill`, `Iter`, and `Let` spec types must be exposed as public names within the library's main namespace. These specs enable automatic mode selection, default value filling, streaming iteration, and variable capture respectively."
    },
    {
      "id": "m33",
      "text": "The `Invoke` spec type must provide a concise and readable string representation when its `repr` is called, specifically shortening the output for nested expressions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m34",
      "text": "The `Invoke` spec type must expose its arguments via a documented method or attribute rather than a private attribute, ensuring stable access to invocation details. The module-level constant previously known as `consts` must now be accessible as `constants`."
    },
    {
      "id": "m44",
      "text": "The `Fill` spec type must implement a meaningful `__repr__` method that clearly indicates its purpose and any provided default value."
    },
    {
      "id": "m45",
      "text": "The `Assign` spec type and the `assign` convenience function must both have clear and informative string representations via their `__repr__` methods."
    },
    {
      "id": "m46",
      "text": "The `Coalesce` spec type must provide a reasonable string representation that reflects its fallback behavior. The `Inspect` class must also maintain a clear representation for debugging purposes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m47",
      "text": "All public specifier types, including `Auto` and `Check`, must have reasonable and descriptive `__repr__` implementations to aid in debugging and introspection."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names listed above are correctly exported and behave as described. Pay special attention to the repr improvements for better developer experience during debugging."
}
